# ThreadSanitizer suppressions for the test run (see TSAN_OPTIONS in the tsan test preset).
#
# trantor (Drogon's network library, v1.5.28) shutdown race: EventLoop::quit() wakes a loop through
# its eventfd while the loop's thread, which already saw the quit flag, exits and closes that
# eventfd in ~EventLoop (thread-local destructor). It happens once per Drogon test executable, at
# the end of the run, and lives entirely in the dependency (the report shows either the close of the
# eventfd or the freeing of the loop, against quit()). Only stacks that contain one of these two
# trantor functions are matched, so races in this project's code are still reported.
race:trantor::EventLoop::~EventLoop
race:trantor::EventLoop::quit
